The decision is of  retrospective operation, as it has not been laid  down that it would operate prospectively;
 moreso, in the case of reversal of the judgment.
 This Court in P.V.George and Ors. v. State  of Kerala and Ors. [2007 (3) SCC 557 : (AIR  2007 SC 1034 in paras 19 and 29)] held  that the law declared by a court will have  a retrospective effect if not declared so  specifically.
